<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Zivno Investicni 1996 profit up.</title>
<headline>Czech Zivno Investicni 1996 profit up.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech investment fund Zivnobanka Prvni Investicni a.s. said on Tuesday it posted an audited net profit of 83.3 million crowns last year, after a 71.3 million net profit in 1995.</p>
<p>The fund, which is managed by a unit of Zivnostenska Banka a.s., also said it would propose general meeting to pay a 20 crown gross dividend per share on the 1996 earnings. The fund is listed on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Further details were not yet available.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
